2
00:07:16,800 --> 00:07:22,800
The Human Centipede (First Sequence) is a horror film directed by Tom Six.

3
00:10:55,200 --> 00:11:01,200
During a stopover in Germany in the middle of a carefree road trip through Europe, two American
girls find themselves alone at night when their car breaks down in the woods.

4
00:14:33,600 --> 00:14:39,600
Searching for help at a nearby villa, they are wooed into the clutches of a
deranged retired surgeon, who has a very disturbed vision.

5
00:18:12,000 --> 00:18:18,000
Dr. Heiter, played by Dieter Laser.

6
00:21:50,400 --> 00:21:56,400
Lindsay, played by Ashley C. Williams.

7
00:25:28,799 --> 00:25:34,799
Jenny, played by Ashlynn Yennie.

8
00:29:07,200 --> 00:29:13,200
Katsuro, played by Akihiro Kitamura.

9
00:32:45,600 --> 00:32:51,600
Detective Kranz, played by Andreas Leupold.

10
00:36:24,000 --> 00:36:30,000
Detective Voller, played by Peter Blankenstein.

11
00:40:02,400 --> 00:40:08,400
The Human Centipede (First Sequence) is a 2009 Dutch body horror
film written, directed and co-produced by Tom Six.

12
00:43:40,800 --> 00:43:46,800
The independent film concerns a deranged German surgeon who kidnaps three tourists and
conjoins them surgically, mouth to anus, forming the eponymous "human centipede".

13
00:47:19,200 --> 00:47:25,200
It stars Dieter Laser as Josef Heiter, the creator
of the centipede; and Ashley C.

14
00:50:57,599 --> 00:51:03,599
Williams, Ashlynn Yennie, and Akihiro Kitamura as Heiter's victims.

15
00:54:36,000 --> 00:54:42,000
According to Six, the concept arose from a joke he had made with friends about punishing a
child molester by stitching his mouth to the anus of a "fat truck driver".

16
00:58:14,400 --> 00:58:20,400
Other sources of inspiration were Nazi medical experiments performed during World War II,
such as those performed by Josef Mengele at the Auschwitz concentration camp.

17
01:01:52,800 --> 01:01:58,800
When approaching investors to fund the project, Six did not mention the premise of the film for fear of putting
off potential backers; financiers did not discover the full nature of the film until completion.

18
01:05:31,200 --> 01:05:37,200
The film held its premiere at the London FrightFest
Film Festival on 30 August 2009.

19
01:09:09,600 --> 01:09:15,600
It received a limited theatrical release in the United States on 30 April 2010.

20
01:12:48,000 --> 01:12:54,000
Despite a mixed critical reception, the film won several
accolades at international film festivals.

21
01:16:26,400 --> 01:16:32,400
Two sequels that were also written and directed by Six—Full Sequence and
Final Sequence—were released in 2011 and 2015, respectively.

22
01:20:04,800 --> 01:20:10,800
The entire trilogy was combined into a single film in 2016, titled Complete Sequence, which Six described as a "movie
centipede" due to each Sequence leading into its successor while simultaneously working as a separate standalone film.

23
01:23:43,199 --> 01:23:49,199
The film explores themes of sadism, kidnapping,
exploitation, surgeon, body mutilation.

24
01:27:21,600 --> 01:27:27,600
The tone is dark.
